  "summary": "Reconciled all five St. Brigid discharges under RBC-TOC-02. Each patient has a progress note, and three have an addendum because results or documents arrived while I worked (§8).\n\n**Walter Kim (pt-0005)**\n- Furosemide: changed from 20 mg daily to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001), per the signed addendum doc-00009.\n- Potassium chloride: stopped, per the discharge summary.\n- Pantoprazole was an inpatient formulary substitution, so he stays on home omeprazole and no pantoprazole was ordered.\n- Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin continue unchanged.\n- Lisinopril: I first kept it held because the 10/21 potassium was 5.4. The 10/23 repeat BMP (K 4.7, creatinine 1.21) met the discharge condition, so I resumed it (mr-00072).\n- Task task-t0003, created while lisinopril was held, is no longer needed. I couldn't close it from here, so I messaged you that it can be closed.\n- An unsigned draft addendum (furosemide 60 mg twice daily) also arrived. I did not act on it because only a signed addendum counts.\n\n**Terence Stark (pt-0004)**\n- Carvedilol: I first raised it to 12.5 mg twice daily per the summary. A signed addendum then arrived reversing the increase (heart rate 48–52, lightheaded on standing), so it is back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0017).\n- Aspirin and insulin 70/30 continue unchanged.\n- **Flagged to you:**\n  - Atorvastatin 80 mg: fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission, so he likely isn't taking it as prescribed. I made no change.\n  - Glipizide 5 mg: an outside prescriber (Dr. Desai) is filling it, and the discharge summary doesn't mention it. I made no change.\n\n**Earnest Roberts (pt-0044)**\n- Lisinopril 20 mg: I resumed it on the 10/22 labs (creatinine 1.08, K 4.6). A potassium of 5.5 on 10/23 then arrived, so I put it back on hold (mr-00373).\n- Task task-t0018 is yours, due 10/26, to review the repeat potassium.\n- Insulin glargine, insulin lispro and rosuvastatin continue unchanged.\n\n**Gerald Whitcomb (pt-0069)**\n- Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (mr-69003): post-discharge creatinine 1.12 met the condition and K was 4.4 on 10/21.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continue unchanged.\n- The discharge plan also calls for a potassium 3 days after discharge (Northgate, results to Riverbend). It isn't in the chart yet.\n\n**Lorraine Pruitt (pt-0067)**\n- Metformin ER stays on hold. The only creatinine on file (1.21) was drawn in hospital on the morning of discharge, and the condition requires a post-discharge result.\n- Task task-t0013 is yours, due 10/24, when the post-discharge BMP is expected.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continue unchanged.\n\nI closed the four new inbox items for these patients and linked the orders and notes. Nothing else new has arrived for them.",
